From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:26:05 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: describe the xRX500 switch macros' interrupt

Each of the two switch macros raises one shared interrupt and neither node
said so. The line aggregates everything the macro can report: the buffer
manager, the parser and classification engine, the MAC block, and the store
and fetch DMA blocks. The two macros use different numbers.

No driver takes it. This switch reaches the same state by polling, so
nothing changes at run time; what it buys is a device tree that describes
the block rather than the subset the current driver happens to use.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
index 7a86b6047528..1e074c44e4a5 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
@@ -279,10 +279,17 @@ ebu_nand: nand-controller@16f00000 {
 	 * own, and neither is shared with anything else on the die. The two
 	 * macros sit on different branches of that PLL, which is why the pair
 	 * differs between them.
+	 *
+	 * One line each aggregates everything the macro can report: the buffer
+	 * manager, the parser and classification engine, the MAC block and the
+	 * store and fetch DMA blocks. Nothing takes it yet; the driver reaches
+	 * the same state by polling.
 	 */
 	gswl: switch@1c000000 {
 		compatible = "lantiq,xrx500-gswip";
 		reg = <0x1c000000 0x4000>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SHARED 48 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		clocks = <&cgu CLK_GSWIP>, <&cgu GCLK_GSWIP>;
 		clock-names = "freq", "gate";
 		dsa,member = <0 0>;
@@ -314,6 +321,8 @@ fixed-link {
 	gswr: switch@1a000000 {
 		compatible = "lantiq,xrx500-gswip-r";
 		reg = <0x1a000000 0x4000>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SHARED 45 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		clocks = <&cgu CLK_PAE>, <&cgu GCLK_PAE>;
 		clock-names = "freq", "gate";
 		dsa,member = <1 0>;
